sejm-stats-439117-39efc9d2f8b8.json
backups/sejmograf_public_*.dump
# supagraf data fixtures: too large for git (~190MB JSON + PDFs).
# Anchored to repo root so source modules under supagraf/fixtures/ stay tracked.
# We can't use `/fixtures/` as a directory ignore (blocks negation of nested
# paths); pattern the contents instead so we can re-include curation files.
/fixtures/*
# Exception: mp_office_expenses/_index.json is curation data (manually-edited
# list of {term, mp_id, year, pdf_url} pairs, ≤460 rows). Lives in /fixtures/
# only because that's where the fetcher reads from; not large data.
!/fixtures/sejm/
/fixtures/sejm/*
!/fixtures/sejm/mp_office_expenses/
# All per-MP fixtures are tracked too (≈2 MB total; derived from scripts/
# bootstrap_jakglosuja_expenses.py + Phase 2 OCR+LLM via supagraf/fetch/).
# Lets CI / fresh clones load straight to the DB without re-running the
# pipeline. mp_office_expenses_quarantine/ is the LLM-extracted set that
# failed validation (scripts/validate_mp_office_expense_fixtures.py) —
# intentionally NOT tracked; those are scratch files for offline re-extract.
!/fixtures/sejm/mp_office_expenses/_index.json
!/fixtures/sejm/mp_office_expenses/t*_*.json
*.log
